@@ chapter-1
It was like this.

[verse.mirror.jabberwocky.v10,margin-top=58.0pt,margin-bottom=59.3pt]
____
                [.tight]#[.title]#JABBERWOCKY.# ’Twas brillig, and the slithy toves Did gyre and gimble in the wabe; All mimsy were the borogoves, And the mome raths outgrabe.#
____

She puzzled over this for some time, but
at last a bright thought struck her. “Why,
it’s a Looking-glass book, of course! And if
I hold it up to a glass, the words will all go
the right way again.”
=>
// tag::mirror[]
It was like this.

[verse.mirror.jabberwocky.v10,margin-top=18.4pt,margin-bottom=0]
____
                             [.title]#JABBERWOCKY.#
____

[verse.mirror.jabberwocky.v10.lh130,margin-top=10.0pt,margin-bottom=33.4pt]
____
                 ’Twas brillig, and the slithy toves
                   Did gyre and gimble in the wabe;
                All mimsy were the borogoves,
                     And the mome raths outgrabe.
____

She puzzled over this for some time, but
at last a bright thought struck her. “Why,
it’s a Looking-glass book, of course! And if
I hold it up to a glass, the words will all go
the right way again.”
// end::mirror[]
